{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W6TwQJLMqWK3fhbH5Eykao","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\"command\":\"epic-review\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"pass\",\"result\":{\"outcome\":\"pass\",\"canonicalReview\":{\"outcome\":\"pass\",\"reviewerLabels\":[\"epic-reviewer-1\",\"epic-reviewer-2\"],\"reconciliationSummary\":\"Both independent reviewers (epic-reviewer-1/claude-fable-5, epic-reviewer-2/gpt-5.5) returned pass with zero blocking findings, and their evidence is mutually consistent. The canonical pass independently re-verified every non-blocking finding against the current tree: package.json lines 27/29 confirm verify and verify-all are textually identical; src/inference/prompts/index.ts defines PROMPT_REGISTRY and DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES while src/index.ts re-exports only sdk.js and sdk.ts imports the registry solely for validation (line 343), confirming no exported name catalog; src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:85-88 confirms the sequential composeTurnRendering→projectLowerBand calls in one work item; test/inference-real.test.ts:120,178 confirms describe.runIf gating alongside the single accounting line built in test/fixtures/openrouter-call.ts:54-55; epic.md:3 still reads 'Status: Draft — pending review'; and team-impl-log.md retains 'Final Gate Status: not-run' (line 142) and the obsolete 'Story 5 BLOCKED awaiting LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY' open-risk note (line 146) despite the keyed-run receipt at line 109. The epic gate was re-run independently: exit 0, 40 test files, 377 passed, 9 env-gated keyed skips, exactly one visible 'NOT-RAN: real-inference (LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY unset)' line — matching both reviewers' gate reports. Reviewer-1's E05-NB-5 (epic.md Draft header) and reviewer-2's E05-NB-001 (stale team-impl-log closeout text) share a root cause and fix scope and are merged into one canonical finding. The only wording-level divergence between reviewers — the test plan's 'suite-level guard, not per-test skips' versus the implemented describe.runIf skips — is retained as a cosmetic observation since the run/not-run state remains one fact reported once. Ruling-020, flagged in the team-impl-log for epic-review ratification, is hereby ratified: the conditional landing-window exception (protected trailing turnless groups after the newest closed turn may lawfully leave the zone above target) is consistent with TC-5.2's already-sanctioned oversized-newest exception, is documented in the tech design's Flow 5 conditional-landing paragraph, and is enforced by implementation and tests; the absolute landing-window sentence in epic.md AC-5.3 should pick up the same qualifier at acceptance (folded into the stale-docs quick-fix finding).\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Story 2 → Story 3 seam handoff is coherent: createSdk's resolveInferenceProvider (src/sdk.ts:313) validates XOR, all seven FORM_KINDS by iterating the exported union, unknown kind keys, non-empty provider/model strings, and PROMPT_REGISTRY membership (src/sdk.ts:343), then drops the adapter into the same resolved.provider slot direct injection uses — everything downstream is unchanged Epic 02 code.\",\"Story 3 → Story 4 reason-format coupling is consistent and ruling-backed: the adapter formats retryable reasons 'provider_failure: <kind>: <message>' and terminal reasons kind-led; the team-impl-log records the approved spec-deviation ruling, Story 4's classification tests consume the same format, and the queue's failAttempt/failTerminal copy the reason verbatim at exhaustion so forms land with the provider_failure-led reason AC-3.2 requires.\",\"Story 4's machinery-untouched claim holds: FAILURE_CLASSIFICATION and safeCall live entirely in src/inference/classify.ts; the work-queue retains its Epic 02 shape with no inference-aware branches, satisfying the Chunk-4 exit gate (Epic 02 derivation suites green untouched).\",\"Story 5 reuses Story 2's seam-conformance helpers parameterized over both hosts per DD-13: assertModelCallContract and assertRoutingThroughSdk run unchanged against the OpenRouter host, and the keyed receipt exists (2026-06-12, openai/gpt-4o-mini, 13/13 pass, 'RAN: real-inference' accounting line, run twice).\",\"Story 6 (boundary) and Story 1 (retirement) are cleanly independent of the inference pipeline as designed; the pipeline gate keeps the Epic 03 registration site, advance-before-poke order, and throw isolation untouched while gating on a turn_end-committed flag.\",\"Provenance flows one direction across stories: stamped from config-known strings in the adapter, copied — never authored — by the messages handler and all three turns-side form writes (src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:101-104, 122-124); the deterministic provider sets none.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"Module architecture matches the tech design exactly: src/inference/{types,classify,adapter,prompts/*} exist as specified; the seven prompt modules are name-keyed in PROMPT_REGISTRY with versioned names; smoothing-v1 is the settled POC port and the other six carry pre-dial-in markers per AC-2.3.\",\"The inference/ ↛ domains/ boundary rule is enforced in scripts/check-boundaries.mjs (independently confirmed: inference/ is grouped with tech-utils/shared in the may-not-import-domains check); inference/ imports only shared/ types, keeping the runtime graph one-directional.\",\"DD-6/DD-7 resolved as designed: safeCall owns the per-call timeout (Promise.race, default 60_000) classifying as retryable timeout; summarizeToolResult input bounding is head-and-tail with marker under maxInputChars (default 200_000), applied before prompt rendering.\",\"Flow 5 matches the design's conditional landing-window contract: advanceDecision is a pure function with whole-turn grouping (NULL turn_id degrading to singleton groups per DD-10), peek-ahead stop, open-turn exclusion from candidacy, and newest-closed-turn protection that structurally protects trailing turnless singletons; the shared-WHERE-clause invariant between status sum and decision walk holds, and the forward-only guard is in the UPDATE itself. Ruling-020 governing the landing-window exception is ratified by this review.\",\"AC-5.4 lands fully: VisibilityBudgets is two-field with 64000/32000 defaults, maxTokens > targetTokens validated with a naming TypeError, and the retired floorTokens is rejected as unknown config citing the Epic 05 retirement.\",\"Provider arrival is injection-only at createSdk: no bin in the package manifest, src/providers/registry.ts and src/cli are absent, and no LHC_PROVIDER, --provider, OpenRouter, or fetch path exists in production code; construction errors are TypeErrors naming the violated rule per the §Error Contract.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"All 22 ACs and 15 TCs across 6 flows trace to implementation and tests with a primary story owner in stories/coverage.md: the construction matrix parameterizes over FORM_KINDS, adversarial wrong-outcome canned text proves mechanical stamping, goldens exist for all seven templates, classification is asserted as data, golden G2 (30k/25k/20k/15k under 64k/32k landing at 35k) is implemented verbatim with the exact-target and oversized-newest legs, and retirement.test.ts proves the export snapshot, no bin, and zero LHC_PROVIDER/--provider references with the retired env var actively set.\",\"Epic gate independently re-run by this canonical pass: verify-all exits 0 with 40 test files, 377 passed, 9 skipped — the 9 skips are exactly the env-gated keyed legs, with the single visible 'NOT-RAN: real-inference (LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY unset)' accounting line per AC-4.1.\",\"The test plan's epic-acceptance condition for the capstone is satisfied: the team-impl-log records the DoD keyed-run receipt (2026-06-12, openai/gpt-4o-mini, 13/13 pass, exactly one 'RAN: real-inference' line, run twice, verbose log retained), so the AC-4.2 integration-readiness gate has been exercised against a real endpoint.\",\"The Epic 03 amendment ledger was applied (floor legs superseded by newest-turn protection, per-intake legs inverted to mid-turn-never-moves, G1 re-cut for turn grouping, floorTokens-rejection test added) and the red-manifest regenerated per the Story 6 commit; the Epic 04 parity-gap deviation note required by Flow 6 is recorded in the team-impl-log.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"No fake adapters, shims, or placeholders in the production path: src/ contains no TODO/FIXME/not-implemented markers, no process.env reads, and no fetch calls — all network code lives in the test-owned OpenRouter fixture as the NFR requires.\",\"All scripted/recording/throwing/hanging ModelCall fakes live in test/fixtures/model-call.ts, the spec-designated mock boundary for Flows 1–3 — boundary mocks, not internal mocks, per the testing strategy.\",\"The deterministic marker-string provider survives only as the explicitly-injected CI test provider (DD-12); it cannot arrive silently — provider arrival is strict XOR injection at createSdk with no defaults, no registry, and no env fallback, verified by retirement.test.ts with LHC_PROVIDER actively set.\",\"The OpenRouter ModelCall host is test-owned by design (DD-13, AC-4.1) — the proof-of-seam second host, not a production shim; the production host (PI extension) is explicitly out of scope for this epic.\",\"The adapter's empty-output rule is enforced in the production path (whitespace-trimmed text rejected as retryable empty_output before any form lands ready), provenance is mechanically copied from config strings and never parsed from model output, and compact/pull/status/inspect/thread-view boundary code never invoke the model-call function.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"E05-NB-1\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"verify and verify-all are now textually identical scripts\",\"evidence\":\"Independently confirmed: package.json lines 27 and 29 both define 'pnpm run red-verify && vitest run'. The convergence is spec-sanctioned (DD-12 dropped the LHC_PROCESS_SUITE gate and the inference suite is env-gated inside the default runner), but two independently maintained identical definitions can drift apart silently; aliasing one to the other would pin the intent.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/package.json\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-6.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E05-NB-2\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Prompt names are config-selectable strings with no exported name catalog\",\"evidence\":\"Independently confirmed: PROMPT_REGISTRY and DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES live in src/inference/prompts/index.ts; src/index.ts re-exports only sdk.js, and sdk.ts imports PROMPT_REGISTRY solely for construction validation (src/sdk.ts:343) without re-exporting it. A host must learn valid prompt names from documentation; unknown names fail construction loudly per AC-1.3 so the fail-loudly posture holds, but the PI extension PRD should account for how operators discover the seven default names.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/inference/prompts/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.3\",\"AC-2.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E05-NB-3\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"title\":\"Turn-derivation work item re-runs the rendering call when only the projection fails\",\"evidence\":\"Independently confirmed at src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:85-88: composeTurnRendering and projectLowerBand are two sequential provider calls in one work item, so a retryable projection failure retries the whole item and re-invokes the rendering call. This is pre-existing Epic 02 work-item granularity, but under real inference each retry now costs a redundant real model call, bounded by the retry budget. Worth weighing during dial-in if projection failures prove common.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E05-NB-4\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Real-suite gating uses describe.runIf skips alongside the single accounting line\",\"evidence\":\"Independently confirmed: test/inference-real.test.ts gates keyed legs with describe.runIf(keyed) (lines 120, 178) while the env is resolved once and exactly one ran/not-ran accounting line is emitted (test/fixtures/openrouter-call.ts:54-55; confirmed as the single 'NOT-RAN: real-inference (LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY unset)' line in the re-run gate output). The test plan's wording was 'a suite-level guard, not per-test skips'; the run/not-run state remains one fact reported once and the 9 vitest skipped entries add runner-level visibility rather than hiding anything, so the AC-4.1 intent is met — noting the cosmetic divergence from the plan's wording.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/test/inference-real.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/fixtures/openrouter-call.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E05-NB-5\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Pack closeout status text is stale ahead of acceptance (merges epic-reviewer-2's E05-NB-001)\",\"evidence\":\"Independently confirmed: epic.md line 3 reads 'Status: Draft — pending review' while all six stories are implemented, gated, and logged complete; team-impl-log.md's Epic Closeout section still reads 'Epic Review Status: not-started' and 'Final Gate Status: not-run' (lines 137-142), and Open Risks retains the obsolete 'Story 5 BLOCKED awaiting LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY' note (line 146) despite the keyed-run receipt recorded at line 109. The closeout fields are expected to update as this review process completes, but the BLOCKED note is factually obsolete now. At the same reconciliation pass, epic.md AC-5.3's absolute landing-window sentence should pick up the conditional qualifier from ruling-020 (ratified by this review), which the tech design's Flow 5 conditional-landing paragraph already documents.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/epic.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/team-impl-log.md\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.1\",\"AC-4.2\",\"AC-5.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Prompt/model dial-in findings are an explicit pre-acceptance backfill obligation for this pack (epic §Out of Scope, tech design §Deferred Items) — plumbing is proven but the tuned prompts and model assignments do not exist yet by design.\",\"The capstone keyed run was executed locally and recorded in the impl log (2026-06-12, openai/gpt-4o-mini, 13/13, run twice); it cannot gate CI by design (no secret in CI), so future regressions in the keyed path are detectable only by re-running the keyed suite manually.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"},\"verifierResults\":[{\"resultId\":\"f86940e7-29ec-4a77-a39e-90fbc4c684ab\",\"outcome\":\"pass\",\"provider\":\"claude-code\",\"model\":\"claude-fable-5\",\"reviewerLabel\":\"epic-reviewer-1\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Story 2 → Story 3 seam handoff is coherent: createSdk's resolveInferenceProvider (src/sdk.ts:313-359) validates XOR, all seven FORM_KINDS (iterating the exported union per the Chunk-2 risk note, never a literal list), unknown kind keys, non-empty provider/model strings, and PROMPT_REGISTRY membership, then drops the adapter into the same resolved.provider slot direct injection uses — everything downstream is unchanged Epic 02 code.\",\"Story 3 → Story 4 reason-format coupling is consistent and ruling-backed: the adapter formats retryable reasons as 'provider_failure: <kind>: <message>' and terminal reasons kind-led (src/inference/adapter.ts:47-55); the team-impl-log records the approved spec-deviation ruling for this format, and Story 4's classification tests consume the same format. The queue (failAttempt/failTerminal in src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts:350-417) copies the reason verbatim at exhaustion, so forms land with the 'provider_failure'-led reason AC-3.2 requires under the established code-before-first-colon convention.\",\"Story 4's machinery-untouched claim verified: FAILURE_CLASSIFICATION and safeCall live entirely in src/inference/classify.ts; the work-queue's failAttempt/failTerminal retain their Epic 02 shape (retryable backoff within budget, terminal immediate, attempts/lastError copied to form metadata) with no inference-aware branches.\",\"Story 5 reuses Story 2's seam-conformance helpers parameterized over both hosts per DD-13: test/inference-real.test.ts runs assertModelCallContract and assertRoutingThroughSdk (the same helpers the fake-host tests run) against the OpenRouter host unchanged.\",\"Story 6 (boundary) and Story 1 (retirement) are cleanly independent of the inference pipeline as designed; the pipeline gate (src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:152-168, 219) keeps the Epic 03 registration site, advance-before-poke order, and throw isolation untouched while gating on a batchCommittedTurnEnd flag that skipped duplicate turn_end events never set.\",\"Provenance flows one direction across stories: stamped from config-known strings in the adapter (src/inference/adapter.ts:91-99), copied — never authored — by the messages handler (src/domains/messages/internal/handlers.ts:61-72) and all three turns-side form writes (src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:101-104, 122-124, 201-203); the deterministic provider sets none (src/providers/deterministic.ts).\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"Module architecture matches the tech design exactly: src/inference/{types,classify,adapter,prompts/*} exist as specified; the seven prompt modules are name-keyed in PROMPT_REGISTRY with versioned names; smoothing-v1 is marked SETTLED (POC port) and the other six carry PRE-DIAL-IN markers per AC-2.3.\",\"The inference/ ↛ domains/ boundary rule was added to scripts/check-boundaries.mjs (lines 117-155) as the tech design required; inference/ imports only shared/ types, and the shared/derivation.ts → inference/types.ts import is type-only and documented as erased at build, keeping the runtime graph one-directional.\",\"DD-6/DD-7 resolved as designed: safeCall owns the per-call timeout (Promise.race with timer cleanup, default 60_000) classifying as retryable 'timeout'; input bounding for summarizeToolResult is head-and-tail with marker under maxInputChars (default 200_000), applied before prompt rendering, with a correct degenerate path when the bound is smaller than the marker itself.\",\"Flow 5 implementation matches the design's conditional landing-window contract: advanceDecision (src/domains/thread-view/internal/boundary.ts:157-195) is a pure function with whole-turn grouping (NULL turn_id degrading to singleton groups per DD-10), peek-ahead stop (remaining − group ≥ target), open-turn exclusion from candidacy while its tokens count in the sum, and newest-closed-turn protection that structurally protects trailing turnless singletons; the shared-WHERE-clause invariant between visibilityZoneTokens and readZoneToolResults holds, and the forward-only guard is in the UPDATE itself.\",\"AC-5.4 lands fully: VisibilityBudgets is two-field with 64000/32000 defaults (src/domains/thread-view/internal/profiles.ts:35-38), maxTokens > targetTokens validated with a naming TypeError, and the retired floorTokens is explicitly rejected as unknown config with a message citing the Epic 05 retirement.\",\"Construction error contract matches §Error Contract: all violations are TypeErrors naming the violated rule ('exactly one of provider or inference', 'missing kind <kind>', 'names unknown template', 'maxTokens must be greater than targetTokens').\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"All 22 ACs across 6 flows trace to implementation and tests. Flow 1: TC-1.1 parameterizes the construction matrix over FORM_KINDS (test/inference-construction.test.ts:64); TC-1.2 routing via recordingCall lanes. Flow 2: TC-2.1 includes the adversarial wrong-outcome canned text (test/inference-adapter.test.ts:45-49, 142); TC-2.2 goldens exist for all seven templates (test/goldens/prompts/); TC-2.3 empty-output retry and exhaustion legs present. Flow 3: TC-3.1 asserts FAILURE_CLASSIFICATION as data matching AC-3.1 exactly; TC-3.2 covers thrown-exception containment and the hangingCall timeout leg. Flow 5: golden G2 implemented verbatim (30k/25k/20k/15k under 64k/32k landing at 35k), exact-target boundary condition, oversized-newest protection, and the trailing-turnless-singleton protection leg. Flow 6: retirement.test.ts proves the export snapshot, no bin, deleted files, and zero LHC_PROVIDER/--provider references with the retired env var actively set.\",\"Epic gate verify-all exits 0: 40 test files, 377 passed, 9 skipped — the 9 skips are exactly the env-gated keyed legs (2 round-trip/conformance + 7 capstone), with the single visible 'NOT-RAN: real-inference (LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY unset)' accounting line per AC-4.1.\",\"The test plan's epic-acceptance condition for the capstone is satisfied: the team-impl-log records the DoD keyed-run receipt — date 2026-06-12, model openai/gpt-4o-mini, 13/13 pass, exactly one 'RAN: real-inference' accounting line, run twice — so the integration-readiness gate (AC-4.2) has actually been exercised against a real endpoint, not just defined.\",\"The Epic 03 amendment ledger was applied (view-boundary.test.ts amended for two-field budgets, mid-turn-never-moves inversions, re-cut G1; floorTokens-rejection test added in view-fixture.test.ts) and the red-manifest regenerated per the Story 6 commit.\",\"The Epic 04 parity-gap deviation note required by Flow 6 is recorded in the team-impl-log (spawned inspect-health parity backfilled pre-Epic-05; spawned-process parity surface deleted instead of carried forward).\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"No fake adapters, shims, or placeholders in the production path. src/ contains zero TODO/FIXME/not-implemented markers (the only 'placeholder' hits are SQL bind-parameter builders), zero process.env reads, and zero fetch calls — the production path is fully real, and all network code lives in the test-owned OpenRouter fixture as the NFR requires.\",\"All scripted/recording/throwing/hanging ModelCall fakes live in test/fixtures/model-call.ts (test code), which is the spec-designated mock boundary for Flows 1–3 — boundary mocks, not internal mocks, per the testing strategy.\",\"The deterministic marker-string provider survives only as the explicitly-injected CI test provider (src/providers/deterministic.ts, DD-12); it cannot arrive silently — provider arrival is strict XOR injection at createSdk with no defaults, no registry, and no env fallback (verified by retirement.test.ts with LHC_PROVIDER actively set in the environment).\",\"The OpenRouter ModelCall host is test-owned by design (DD-13, AC-4.1) — it is the proof-of-seam second host, not a production shim; the production host (PI extension) is explicitly out of scope for this epic.\",\"The adapter's empty-output rule is enforced in the production path (whitespace-trimmed text rejected as retryable empty_output before any form can land ready), and provenance is mechanically copied from config strings, never parsed from model output.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"E05-NB-1\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"verify and verify-all are now textually identical scripts\",\"evidence\":\"package.json defines both 'verify' and 'verify-all' as 'pnpm run red-verify && vitest run'. The convergence is spec-sanctioned (the process-suite gate left verify-all and the inference suite is env-gated inside the default runner), but two independently-maintained identical definitions can drift apart silently; aliasing one to the other would pin the intent.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/package.json\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-6.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E05-NB-2\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Prompt names are config-selectable strings with no exported name catalog\",\"evidence\":\"PROMPT_REGISTRY and DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES (src/inference/prompts/index.ts) are construction internals not exported from the package entry (the retirement snapshot confirms the SDK-only surface). A host must learn valid prompt names from documentation; unknown names fail construction loudly per AC-1.3, so the fail-loudly posture holds, but the PI extension PRD should account for how operators discover the seven default names.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/inference/prompts/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.3\",\"AC-2.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E05-NB-3\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"title\":\"Turn-derivation work item re-runs the rendering call when only the projection fails\",\"evidence\":\"turnDerivationHandler (src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:85-88) makes two sequential provider calls (composeTurnRendering then projectLowerBand) in one work item; a retryable projection failure retries the whole item, re-invoking the rendering call. This is pre-existing Epic 02 work-item granularity, but under real inference each retry now costs a redundant real model call, bounded by the retry budget. Worth weighing during dial-in if projection failures prove common.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E05-NB-4\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Real-suite gating uses describe.runIf skips alongside the single accounting line\",\"evidence\":\"The test plan said the accounting rule is 'a suite-level guard, not per-test skips'; the implementation resolves the env once at module load and emits exactly one line (the guard), but the keyed legs surface as 9 vitest 'skipped' entries via describe.runIf. The run/not-run state remains one fact reported once and the skips add runner-level visibility rather than hiding anything, so the AC-4.1 intent is met; noting the cosmetic divergence from the plan's wording.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/test/inference-real.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/fixtures/openrouter-call.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E05-NB-5\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Epic document status header still reads Draft\",\"evidence\":\"docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/epic.md line 3 reads 'Status: Draft — pending review' while all six stories are implemented, gated, and logged complete. The pack also carries the planned pre-acceptance backfill dependency (dial-in findings), so the header may be intentional, but it should be reconciled at acceptance.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/epic.md\"],\"requirementIds\":[],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Prompt/model dial-in findings are an explicit pre-acceptance backfill obligation for this pack (epic §Out of Scope, tech design §Deferred Items) — plumbing is proven but the tuned prompts and model assignments do not exist yet by design.\",\"The capstone keyed run was executed locally and recorded in the impl log (2026-06-12, openai/gpt-4o-mini, 13/13); it cannot gate CI by design (no secret in CI), so future regressions in the keyed path are detectable only by re-running the keyed suite manually.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"},{\"resultId\":\"71271197-7285-4976-99c5-59969981a6ac\",\"outcome\":\"pass\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.5\",\"reviewerLabel\":\"epic-reviewer-2\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"The six flows are coherent across the SDK surface: CLI retirement removes package bin/env registry paths, then createSdk accepts exactly one of direct provider or inference config, with assignment validation before construction.\",\"Inference, adapter, classification, and handler writes line up across stories: adapter output flows through the existing DerivationProvider seam and Epic 02 queue machinery; provenance is copied into derived-form metadata by handlers.\",\"The keyed real-inference receipt exists: /tmp/lbuild-run/keyed-run-verbose.txt shows `RAN: real-inference (model openai/gpt-4o-mini)` and 13/13 tests passing; default gates still show visible NOT-RAN accounting when the key is absent.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"Architecture matches the tech design: src/inference implements the semantic adapter layer and imports shared types only; boundary check passes with 97 files checked.\",\"Provider arrival is injection-only at createSdk. package.json has no bin, src/providers/registry.ts and src/cli are absent, and source/dist scans found no LHC_PROVIDER, --provider, OpenRouter, or fetch path in production code.\",\"Turn-end boundary advance is implemented at the existing post-commit seam: intake records a committed turn_end flag, then thread-view advances whole groups using stored token estimates and the configured max/target budgets.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"All 22 ACs and 15 TCs have a primary story owner in stories/coverage.md, and the implemented test suite contains the expected inference, real-suite, boundary, and retirement tests.\",\"Story Gate passed: cd packages/lhc && pnpm run verify completed build, typecheck, lint, boundaries, and vitest with 40 files passed, 377 tests passed, 9 keyed real-inference legs skipped with visible NOT-RAN accounting.\",\"Epic Gate passed: cd packages/lhc && pnpm run verify-all completed the same red-verify and vitest gate successfully.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"No material fake adapter, shim, placeholder, or non-real execution path was found in production inference. Production inference calls only the host-supplied ModelCall through createInferenceProvider; OpenRouter transport is confined to test fixtures.\",\"The deterministic provider remains available only by explicit direct injection, matching the test/default-provider contract; there is no registry or env fallback that silently selects it.\",\"Compact, pull, status, inspect, and thread-view boundary code do not call the model function; inference is confined to drained derivation work.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"E05-NB-001\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Team log has stale closeout/open-risk status text\",\"evidence\":\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/team-impl-log.md records the keyed run receipt at lines 101-113, but still says Final Gate Status: not-run and repeats the old Story 5 BLOCKED note at lines 137-146. Current reviewer gates passed.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/team-impl-log.md\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.1\",\"AC-4.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"}]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/epic/002-epic-review.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-13T00:35:32.393Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-13T00:44:16.701Z\"}\n2\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"95bd8909-1a10-4908-8466-083d4962a667","uuid":"94123881-646f-4857-bd7c-3641a2cb455b","timestamp":"2026-06-13T00:53:12.889Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/epic/002-epic-review.json","content":"{\"command\":\"epic-review\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"pass\",\"result\":{\"outcome\":\"pass\",\"canonicalReview\":{\"outcome\":\"pass\",\"reviewerLabels\":[\"epic-reviewer-1\",\"epic-reviewer-2\"],\"reconciliationSummary\":\"Both independent reviewers (epic-reviewer-1/claude-fable-5, epic-reviewer-2/gpt-5.5) returned pass with zero blocking findings, and their evidence is mutually consistent. The canonical pass independently re-verified every non-blocking finding against the current tree: package.json lines 27/29 confirm verify and verify-all are textually identical; src/inference/prompts/index.ts defines PROMPT_REGISTRY and DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES while src/index.ts re-exports only sdk.js and sdk.ts imports the registry solely for validation (line 343), confirming no exported name catalog; src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:85-88 confirms the sequential composeTurnRendering→projectLowerBand calls in one work item; test/inference-real.test.ts:120,178 confirms describe.runIf gating alongside the single accounting line built in test/fixtures/openrouter-call.ts:54-55; epic.md:3 still reads 'Status: Draft — pending review'; and team-impl-log.md retains 'Final Gate Status: not-run' (line 142) and the obsolete 'Story 5 BLOCKED awaiting LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY' open-risk note (line 146) despite the keyed-run receipt at line 109. The epic gate was re-run independently: exit 0, 40 test files, 377 passed, 9 env-gated keyed skips, exactly one visible 'NOT-RAN: real-inference (LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY unset)' line — matching both reviewers' gate reports. Reviewer-1's E05-NB-5 (epic.md Draft header) and reviewer-2's E05-NB-001 (stale team-impl-log closeout text) share a root cause and fix scope and are merged into one canonical finding. The only wording-level divergence between reviewers — the test plan's 'suite-level guard, not per-test skips' versus the implemented describe.runIf skips — is retained as a cosmetic observation since the run/not-run state remains one fact reported once. Ruling-020, flagged in the team-impl-log for epic-review ratification, is hereby ratified: the conditional landing-window exception (protected trailing turnless groups after the newest closed turn may lawfully leave the zone above target) is consistent with TC-5.2's already-sanctioned oversized-newest exception, is documented in the tech design's Flow 5 conditional-landing paragraph, and is enforced by implementation and tests; the absolute landing-window sentence in epic.md AC-5.3 should pick up the same qualifier at acceptance (folded into the stale-docs quick-fix finding).\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Story 2 → Story 3 seam handoff is coherent: createSdk's resolveInferenceProvider (src/sdk.ts:313) validates XOR, all seven FORM_KINDS by iterating the exported union, unknown kind keys, non-empty provider/model strings, and PROMPT_REGISTRY membership (src/sdk.ts:343), then drops the adapter into the same resolved.provider slot direct injection uses — everything downstream is unchanged Epic 02 code.\",\"Story 3 → Story 4 reason-format coupling is consistent and ruling-backed: the adapter formats retryable reasons 'provider_failure: <kind>: <message>' and terminal reasons kind-led; the team-impl-log records the approved spec-deviation ruling, Story 4's classification tests consume the same format, and the queue's failAttempt/failTerminal copy the reason verbatim at exhaustion so forms land with the provider_failure-led reason AC-3.2 requires.\",\"Story 4's machinery-untouched claim holds: FAILURE_CLASSIFICATION and safeCall live entirely in src/inference/classify.ts; the work-queue retains its Epic 02 shape with no inference-aware branches, satisfying the Chunk-4 exit gate (Epic 02 derivation suites green untouched).\",\"Story 5 reuses Story 2's seam-conformance helpers parameterized over both hosts per DD-13: assertModelCallContract and assertRoutingThroughSdk run unchanged against the OpenRouter host, and the keyed receipt exists (2026-06-12, openai/gpt-4o-mini, 13/13 pass, 'RAN: real-inference' accounting line, run twice).\",\"Story 6 (boundary) and Story 1 (retirement) are cleanly independent of the inference pipeline as designed; the pipeline gate keeps the Epic 03 registration site, advance-before-poke order, and throw isolation untouched while gating on a turn_end-committed flag.\",\"Provenance flows one direction across stories: stamped from config-known strings in the adapter, copied — never authored — by the messages handler and all three turns-side form writes (src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:101-104, 122-124); the deterministic provider sets none.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"Module architecture matches the tech design exactly: src/inference/{types,classify,adapter,prompts/*} exist as specified; the seven prompt modules are name-keyed in PROMPT_REGISTRY with versioned names; smoothing-v1 is the settled POC port and the other six carry pre-dial-in markers per AC-2.3.\",\"The inference/ ↛ domains/ boundary rule is enforced in scripts/check-boundaries.mjs (independently confirmed: inference/ is grouped with tech-utils/shared in the may-not-import-domains check); inference/ imports only shared/ types, keeping the runtime graph one-directional.\",\"DD-6/DD-7 resolved as designed: safeCall owns the per-call timeout (Promise.race, default 60_000) classifying as retryable timeout; summarizeToolResult input bounding is head-and-tail with marker under maxInputChars (default 200_000), applied before prompt rendering.\",\"Flow 5 matches the design's conditional landing-window contract: advanceDecision is a pure function with whole-turn grouping (NULL turn_id degrading to singleton groups per DD-10), peek-ahead stop, open-turn exclusion from candidacy, and newest-closed-turn protection that structurally protects trailing turnless singletons; the shared-WHERE-clause invariant between status sum and decision walk holds, and the forward-only guard is in the UPDATE itself. Ruling-020 governing the landing-window exception is ratified by this review.\",\"AC-5.4 lands fully: VisibilityBudgets is two-field with 64000/32000 defaults, maxTokens > targetTokens validated with a naming TypeError, and the retired floorTokens is rejected as unknown config citing the Epic 05 retirement.\",\"Provider arrival is injection-only at createSdk: no bin in the package manifest, src/providers/registry.ts and src/cli are absent, and no LHC_PROVIDER, --provider, OpenRouter, or fetch path exists in production code; construction errors are TypeErrors naming the violated rule per the §Error Contract.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"All 22 ACs and 15 TCs across 6 flows trace to implementation and tests with a primary story owner in stories/coverage.md: the construction matrix parameterizes over FORM_KINDS, adversarial wrong-outcome canned text proves mechanical stamping, goldens exist for all seven templates, classification is asserted as data, golden G2 (30k/25k/20k/15k under 64k/32k landing at 35k) is implemented verbatim with the exact-target and oversized-newest legs, and retirement.test.ts proves the export snapshot, no bin, and zero LHC_PROVIDER/--provider references with the retired env var actively set.\",\"Epic gate independently re-run by this canonical pass: verify-all exits 0 with 40 test files, 377 passed, 9 skipped — the 9 skips are exactly the env-gated keyed legs, with the single visible 'NOT-RAN: real-inference (LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY unset)' accounting line per AC-4.1.\",\"The test plan's epic-acceptance condition for the capstone is satisfied: the team-impl-log records the DoD keyed-run receipt (2026-06-12, openai/gpt-4o-mini, 13/13 pass, exactly one 'RAN: real-inference' line, run twice, verbose log retained), so the AC-4.2 integration-readiness gate has been exercised against a real endpoint.\",\"The Epic 03 amendment ledger was applied (floor legs superseded by newest-turn protection, per-intake legs inverted to mid-turn-never-moves, G1 re-cut for turn grouping, floorTokens-rejection test added) and the red-manifest regenerated per the Story 6 commit; the Epic 04 parity-gap deviation note required by Flow 6 is recorded in the team-impl-log.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"No fake adapters, shims, or placeholders in the production path: src/ contains no TODO/FIXME/not-implemented markers, no process.env reads, and no fetch calls — all network code lives in the test-owned OpenRouter fixture as the NFR requires.\",\"All scripted/recording/throwing/hanging ModelCall fakes live in test/fixtures/model-call.ts, the spec-designated mock boundary for Flows 1–3 — boundary mocks, not internal mocks, per the testing strategy.\",\"The deterministic marker-string provider survives only as the explicitly-injected CI test provider (DD-12); it cannot arrive silently — provider arrival is strict XOR injection at createSdk with no defaults, no registry, and no env fallback, verified by retirement.test.ts with LHC_PROVIDER actively set.\",\"The OpenRouter ModelCall host is test-owned by design (DD-13, AC-4.1) — the proof-of-seam second host, not a production shim; the production host (PI extension) is explicitly out of scope for this epic.\",\"The adapter's empty-output rule is enforced in the production path (whitespace-trimmed text rejected as retryable empty_output before any form lands ready), provenance is mechanically copied from config strings and never parsed from model output, and compact/pull/status/inspect/thread-view boundary code never invoke the model-call function.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"E05-NB-1\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"verify and verify-all are now textually identical scripts\",\"evidence\":\"Independently confirmed: package.json lines 27 and 29 both define 'pnpm run red-verify && vitest run'. The convergence is spec-sanctioned (DD-12 dropped the LHC_PROCESS_SUITE gate and the inference suite is env-gated inside the default runner), but two independently maintained identical definitions can drift apart silently; aliasing one to the other would pin the intent.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/package.json\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-6.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E05-NB-2\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Prompt names are config-selectable strings with no exported name catalog\",\"evidence\":\"Independently confirmed: PROMPT_REGISTRY and DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES live in src/inference/prompts/index.ts; src/index.ts re-exports only sdk.js, and sdk.ts imports PROMPT_REGISTRY solely for construction validation (src/sdk.ts:343) without re-exporting it. A host must learn valid prompt names from documentation; unknown names fail construction loudly per AC-1.3 so the fail-loudly posture holds, but the PI extension PRD should account for how operators discover the seven default names.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/inference/prompts/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.3\",\"AC-2.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E05-NB-3\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"title\":\"Turn-derivation work item re-runs the rendering call when only the projection fails\",\"evidence\":\"Independently confirmed at src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:85-88: composeTurnRendering and projectLowerBand are two sequential provider calls in one work item, so a retryable projection failure retries the whole item and re-invokes the rendering call. This is pre-existing Epic 02 work-item granularity, but under real inference each retry now costs a redundant real model call, bounded by the retry budget. Worth weighing during dial-in if projection failures prove common.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E05-NB-4\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Real-suite gating uses describe.runIf skips alongside the single accounting line\",\"evidence\":\"Independently confirmed: test/inference-real.test.ts gates keyed legs with describe.runIf(keyed) (lines 120, 178) while the env is resolved once and exactly one ran/not-ran accounting line is emitted (test/fixtures/openrouter-call.ts:54-55; confirmed as the single 'NOT-RAN: real-inference (LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY unset)' line in the re-run gate output). The test plan's wording was 'a suite-level guard, not per-test skips'; the run/not-run state remains one fact reported once and the 9 vitest skipped entries add runner-level visibility rather than hiding anything, so the AC-4.1 intent is met — noting the cosmetic divergence from the plan's wording.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/test/inference-real.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/fixtures/openrouter-call.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E05-NB-5\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Pack closeout status text is stale ahead of acceptance (merges epic-reviewer-2's E05-NB-001)\",\"evidence\":\"Independently confirmed: epic.md line 3 reads 'Status: Draft — pending review' while all six stories are implemented, gated, and logged complete; team-impl-log.md's Epic Closeout section still reads 'Epic Review Status: not-started' and 'Final Gate Status: not-run' (lines 137-142), and Open Risks retains the obsolete 'Story 5 BLOCKED awaiting LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY' note (line 146) despite the keyed-run receipt recorded at line 109. The closeout fields are expected to update as this review process completes, but the BLOCKED note is factually obsolete now. At the same reconciliation pass, epic.md AC-5.3's absolute landing-window sentence should pick up the conditional qualifier from ruling-020 (ratified by this review), which the tech design's Flow 5 conditional-landing paragraph already documents.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/epic.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/team-impl-log.md\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.1\",\"AC-4.2\",\"AC-5.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Prompt/model dial-in findings are an explicit pre-acceptance backfill obligation for this pack (epic §Out of Scope, tech design §Deferred Items) — plumbing is proven but the tuned prompts and model assignments do not exist yet by design.\",\"The capstone keyed run was executed locally and recorded in the impl log (2026-06-12, openai/gpt-4o-mini, 13/13, run twice); it cannot gate CI by design (no secret in CI), so future regressions in the keyed path are detectable only by re-running the keyed suite manually.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"},\"verifierResults\":[{\"resultId\":\"f86940e7-29ec-4a77-a39e-90fbc4c684ab\",\"outcome\":\"pass\",\"provider\":\"claude-code\",\"model\":\"claude-fable-5\",\"reviewerLabel\":\"epic-reviewer-1\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Story 2 → Story 3 seam handoff is coherent: createSdk's resolveInferenceProvider (src/sdk.ts:313-359) validates XOR, all seven FORM_KINDS (iterating the exported union per the Chunk-2 risk note, never a literal list), unknown kind keys, non-empty provider/model strings, and PROMPT_REGISTRY membership, then drops the adapter into the same resolved.provider slot direct injection uses — everything downstream is unchanged Epic 02 code.\",\"Story 3 → Story 4 reason-format coupling is consistent and ruling-backed: the adapter formats retryable reasons as 'provider_failure: <kind>: <message>' and terminal reasons kind-led (src/inference/adapter.ts:47-55); the team-impl-log records the approved spec-deviation ruling for this format, and Story 4's classification tests consume the same format. The queue (failAttempt/failTerminal in src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts:350-417) copies the reason verbatim at exhaustion, so forms land with the 'provider_failure'-led reason AC-3.2 requires under the established code-before-first-colon convention.\",\"Story 4's machinery-untouched claim verified: FAILURE_CLASSIFICATION and safeCall live entirely in src/inference/classify.ts; the work-queue's failAttempt/failTerminal retain their Epic 02 shape (retryable backoff within budget, terminal immediate, attempts/lastError copied to form metadata) with no inference-aware branches.\",\"Story 5 reuses Story 2's seam-conformance helpers parameterized over both hosts per DD-13: test/inference-real.test.ts runs assertModelCallContract and assertRoutingThroughSdk (the same helpers the fake-host tests run) against the OpenRouter host unchanged.\",\"Story 6 (boundary) and Story 1 (retirement) are cleanly independent of the inference pipeline as designed; the pipeline gate (src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:152-168, 219) keeps the Epic 03 registration site, advance-before-poke order, and throw isolation untouched while gating on a batchCommittedTurnEnd flag that skipped duplicate turn_end events never set.\",\"Provenance flows one direction across stories: stamped from config-known strings in the adapter (src/inference/adapter.ts:91-99), copied — never authored — by the messages handler (src/domains/messages/internal/handlers.ts:61-72) and all three turns-side form writes (src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:101-104, 122-124, 201-203); the deterministic provider sets none (src/providers/deterministic.ts).\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"Module architecture matches the tech design exactly: src/inference/{types,classify,adapter,prompts/*} exist as specified; the seven prompt modules are name-keyed in PROMPT_REGISTRY with versioned names; smoothing-v1 is marked SETTLED (POC port) and the other six carry PRE-DIAL-IN markers per AC-2.3.\",\"The inference/ ↛ domains/ boundary rule was added to scripts/check-boundaries.mjs (lines 117-155) as the tech design required; inference/ imports only shared/ types, and the shared/derivation.ts → inference/types.ts import is type-only and documented as erased at build, keeping the runtime graph one-directional.\",\"DD-6/DD-7 resolved as designed: safeCall owns the per-call timeout (Promise.race with timer cleanup, default 60_000) classifying as retryable 'timeout'; input bounding for summarizeToolResult is head-and-tail with marker under maxInputChars (default 200_000), applied before prompt rendering, with a correct degenerate path when the bound is smaller than the marker itself.\",\"Flow 5 implementation matches the design's conditional landing-window contract: advanceDecision (src/domains/thread-view/internal/boundary.ts:157-195) is a pure function with whole-turn grouping (NULL turn_id degrading to singleton groups per DD-10), peek-ahead stop (remaining − group ≥ target), open-turn exclusion from candidacy while its tokens count in the sum, and newest-closed-turn protection that structurally protects trailing turnless singletons; the shared-WHERE-clause invariant between visibilityZoneTokens and readZoneToolResults holds, and the forward-only guard is in the UPDATE itself.\",\"AC-5.4 lands fully: VisibilityBudgets is two-field with 64000/32000 defaults (src/domains/thread-view/internal/profiles.ts:35-38), maxTokens > targetTokens validated with a naming TypeError, and the retired floorTokens is explicitly rejected as unknown config with a message citing the Epic 05 retirement.\",\"Construction error contract matches §Error Contract: all violations are TypeErrors naming the violated rule ('exactly one of provider or inference', 'missing kind <kind>', 'names unknown template', 'maxTokens must be greater than targetTokens').\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"All 22 ACs across 6 flows trace to implementation and tests. Flow 1: TC-1.1 parameterizes the construction matrix over FORM_KINDS (test/inference-construction.test.ts:64); TC-1.2 routing via recordingCall lanes. Flow 2: TC-2.1 includes the adversarial wrong-outcome canned text (test/inference-adapter.test.ts:45-49, 142); TC-2.2 goldens exist for all seven templates (test/goldens/prompts/); TC-2.3 empty-output retry and exhaustion legs present. Flow 3: TC-3.1 asserts FAILURE_CLASSIFICATION as data matching AC-3.1 exactly; TC-3.2 covers thrown-exception containment and the hangingCall timeout leg. Flow 5: golden G2 implemented verbatim (30k/25k/20k/15k under 64k/32k landing at 35k), exact-target boundary condition, oversized-newest protection, and the trailing-turnless-singleton protection leg. Flow 6: retirement.test.ts proves the export snapshot, no bin, deleted files, and zero LHC_PROVIDER/--provider references with the retired env var actively set.\",\"Epic gate verify-all exits 0: 40 test files, 377 passed, 9 skipped — the 9 skips are exactly the env-gated keyed legs (2 round-trip/conformance + 7 capstone), with the single visible 'NOT-RAN: real-inference (LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY unset)' accounting line per AC-4.1.\",\"The test plan's epic-acceptance condition for the capstone is satisfied: the team-impl-log records the DoD keyed-run receipt — date 2026-06-12, model openai/gpt-4o-mini, 13/13 pass, exactly one 'RAN: real-inference' accounting line, run twice — so the integration-readiness gate (AC-4.2) has actually been exercised against a real endpoint, not just defined.\",\"The Epic 03 amendment ledger was applied (view-boundary.test.ts amended for two-field budgets, mid-turn-never-moves inversions, re-cut G1; floorTokens-rejection test added in view-fixture.test.ts) and the red-manifest regenerated per the Story 6 commit.\",\"The Epic 04 parity-gap deviation note required by Flow 6 is recorded in the team-impl-log (spawned inspect-health parity backfilled pre-Epic-05; spawned-process parity surface deleted instead of carried forward).\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"No fake adapters, shims, or placeholders in the production path. src/ contains zero TODO/FIXME/not-implemented markers (the only 'placeholder' hits are SQL bind-parameter builders), zero process.env reads, and zero fetch calls — the production path is fully real, and all network code lives in the test-owned OpenRouter fixture as the NFR requires.\",\"All scripted/recording/throwing/hanging ModelCall fakes live in test/fixtures/model-call.ts (test code), which is the spec-designated mock boundary for Flows 1–3 — boundary mocks, not internal mocks, per the testing strategy.\",\"The deterministic marker-string provider survives only as the explicitly-injected CI test provider (src/providers/deterministic.ts, DD-12); it cannot arrive silently — provider arrival is strict XOR injection at createSdk with no defaults, no registry, and no env fallback (verified by retirement.test.ts with LHC_PROVIDER actively set in the environment).\",\"The OpenRouter ModelCall host is test-owned by design (DD-13, AC-4.1) — it is the proof-of-seam second host, not a production shim; the production host (PI extension) is explicitly out of scope for this epic.\",\"The adapter's empty-output rule is enforced in the production path (whitespace-trimmed text rejected as retryable empty_output before any form can land ready), and provenance is mechanically copied from config strings, never parsed from model output.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"E05-NB-1\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"verify and verify-all are now textually identical scripts\",\"evidence\":\"package.json defines both 'verify' and 'verify-all' as 'pnpm run red-verify && vitest run'. The convergence is spec-sanctioned (the process-suite gate left verify-all and the inference suite is env-gated inside the default runner), but two independently-maintained identical definitions can drift apart silently; aliasing one to the other would pin the intent.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/package.json\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-6.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E05-NB-2\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Prompt names are config-selectable strings with no exported name catalog\",\"evidence\":\"PROMPT_REGISTRY and DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES (src/inference/prompts/index.ts) are construction internals not exported from the package entry (the retirement snapshot confirms the SDK-only surface). A host must learn valid prompt names from documentation; unknown names fail construction loudly per AC-1.3, so the fail-loudly posture holds, but the PI extension PRD should account for how operators discover the seven default names.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/inference/prompts/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.3\",\"AC-2.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E05-NB-3\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"title\":\"Turn-derivation work item re-runs the rendering call when only the projection fails\",\"evidence\":\"turnDerivationHandler (src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:85-88) makes two sequential provider calls (composeTurnRendering then projectLowerBand) in one work item; a retryable projection failure retries the whole item, re-invoking the rendering call. This is pre-existing Epic 02 work-item granularity, but under real inference each retry now costs a redundant real model call, bounded by the retry budget. Worth weighing during dial-in if projection failures prove common.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E05-NB-4\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Real-suite gating uses describe.runIf skips alongside the single accounting line\",\"evidence\":\"The test plan said the accounting rule is 'a suite-level guard, not per-test skips'; the implementation resolves the env once at module load and emits exactly one line (the guard), but the keyed legs surface as 9 vitest 'skipped' entries via describe.runIf. The run/not-run state remains one fact reported once and the skips add runner-level visibility rather than hiding anything, so the AC-4.1 intent is met; noting the cosmetic divergence from the plan's wording.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/test/inference-real.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/fixtures/openrouter-call.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E05-NB-5\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Epic document status header still reads Draft\",\"evidence\":\"docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/epic.md line 3 reads 'Status: Draft — pending review' while all six stories are implemented, gated, and logged complete. The pack also carries the planned pre-acceptance backfill dependency (dial-in findings), so the header may be intentional, but it should be reconciled at acceptance.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/epic.md\"],\"requirementIds\":[],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Prompt/model dial-in findings are an explicit pre-acceptance backfill obligation for this pack (epic §Out of Scope, tech design §Deferred Items) — plumbing is proven but the tuned prompts and model assignments do not exist yet by design.\",\"The capstone keyed run was executed locally and recorded in the impl log (2026-06-12, openai/gpt-4o-mini, 13/13); it cannot gate CI by design (no secret in CI), so future regressions in the keyed path are detectable only by re-running the keyed suite manually.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"},{\"resultId\":\"71271197-7285-4976-99c5-59969981a6ac\",\"outcome\":\"pass\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.5\",\"reviewerLabel\":\"epic-reviewer-2\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"The six flows are coherent across the SDK surface: CLI retirement removes package bin/env registry paths, then createSdk accepts exactly one of direct provider or inference config, with assignment validation before construction.\",\"Inference, adapter, classification, and handler writes line up across stories: adapter output flows through the existing DerivationProvider seam and Epic 02 queue machinery; provenance is copied into derived-form metadata by handlers.\",\"The keyed real-inference receipt exists: /tmp/lbuild-run/keyed-run-verbose.txt shows `RAN: real-inference (model openai/gpt-4o-mini)` and 13/13 tests passing; default gates still show visible NOT-RAN accounting when the key is absent.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"Architecture matches the tech design: src/inference implements the semantic adapter layer and imports shared types only; boundary check passes with 97 files checked.\",\"Provider arrival is injection-only at createSdk. package.json has no bin, src/providers/registry.ts and src/cli are absent, and source/dist scans found no LHC_PROVIDER, --provider, OpenRouter, or fetch path in production code.\",\"Turn-end boundary advance is implemented at the existing post-commit seam: intake records a committed turn_end flag, then thread-view advances whole groups using stored token estimates and the configured max/target budgets.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"All 22 ACs and 15 TCs have a primary story owner in stories/coverage.md, and the implemented test suite contains the expected inference, real-suite, boundary, and retirement tests.\",\"Story Gate passed: cd packages/lhc && pnpm run verify completed build, typecheck, lint, boundaries, and vitest with 40 files passed, 377 tests passed, 9 keyed real-inference legs skipped with visible NOT-RAN accounting.\",\"Epic Gate passed: cd packages/lhc && pnpm run verify-all completed the same red-verify and vitest gate successfully.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"No material fake adapter, shim, placeholder, or non-real execution path was found in production inference. Production inference calls only the host-supplied ModelCall through createInferenceProvider; OpenRouter transport is confined to test fixtures.\",\"The deterministic provider remains available only by explicit direct injection, matching the test/default-provider contract; there is no registry or env fallback that silently selects it.\",\"Compact, pull, status, inspect, and thread-view boundary code do not call the model function; inference is confined to drained derivation work.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"E05-NB-001\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Team log has stale closeout/open-risk status text\",\"evidence\":\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/team-impl-log.md records the keyed run receipt at lines 101-113, but still says Final Gate Status: not-run and repeats the old Story 5 BLOCKED note at lines 137-146. Current reviewer gates passed.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/team-impl-log.md\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.1\",\"AC-4.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"}]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/epic/002-epic-review.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-13T00:35:32.393Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-13T00:44:16.701Z\"}\n","numLines":2,"startLine":1,"totalLines":2}}}
