{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_01U1jBCSKafmY64sWsCWC75u","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both gates pass: exit 0, 40 test files, 377 passed, 9 env-gated keyed skips, exactly one visible NOT-RAN accounting line each. Verification is complete.\n\nWhat I confirmed:\n\n- **Fix batch 001 is fully applied in the working tree** despite its result envelope (`002-fix-result.json`) recording `blocked` — that failure was a CLI output-format error (provider stdout was stream-JSON, not the exact envelope), not a failure of the fixes. E05-NB-1: `verify-all` now delegates to `pnpm run verify`. E05-NB-2: `PROMPT_NAMES` and `DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES` are exported through `src/sdk.ts` with the retirement snapshot intentionally updated per the fix-batch instruction. E05-NB-5: epic.md header updated and AC-5.3 carries the ratified ruling-020 qualifier; the obsolete Story 5 BLOCKED note is replaced with a resolved entry.\n- **No regressions from the fix batch** — the export-surface change is snapshot-pinned, the boundary script change tightens (not weakens) the inference/↛domains/ rule, and both script names survive.\n- **Remaining items are non-blocking**: E05-NB-3 (double model call on projection retry, `derive.ts:85-88`) and E05-NB-4 (describe.runIf gating wording) are unchanged and deferred by canonical ruling; the team-impl-log Epic Closeout block is still stale bookkeeping that closeout itself should update.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"outcome\": \"ready-for-closeout\",\n  \"confirmedIssues\": [\n    \"E05-NB-3 (non-blocking, human-ruling, deferred to dial-in) — confirmed still present: src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:85-88 makes composeTurnRendering and projectLowerBand as two sequential provider calls in one work item, so a retryable projection failure retries the whole item and re-invokes the rendering call at real-model cost, bounded by the retry budget. Out of fix-batch scope by design; carry into the dial-in working period.\",\n    \"E05-NB-4 (non-blocking, cosmetic) — confirmed still present: test/inference-real.test.ts gates keyed legs with describe.runIf(keyed) (lines 120, 178) versus the test plan's 'suite-level guard, not per-test skips' wording; exactly one ran/not-ran accounting line is still emitted (test/fixtures/openrouter-call.ts:54-55, and the single 'NOT-RAN: real-inference (LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY unset)' line appeared once in each re-run gate). AC-4.1 intent met; wording divergence stands.\",\n    \"E05-NB-5 residual (non-blocking, closeout bookkeeping) — team-impl-log.md's Epic Closeout block still reads 'Current Epic Review Artifact: none', 'Epic Review Status: not-started', 'Epic Fix Status: not-started', 'Epic Reverify Status: not-started', 'Final Gate Status: not-run'; these fields track this very review cycle and must be updated as closeout completes. The factually-obsolete Story 5 BLOCKED open-risk note was fixed (replaced with a resolved entry plus the two accepted-risk notes).\"\n  ],\n  \"disputedOrUnconfirmedIssues\": [\n    \"artifacts/fix/002-fix-result.json records status 'blocked' (PROVIDER_OUTPUT_INVALID: provider stdout was stream-JSON, not the exact JSON envelope). Independently verified as a process/transport anomaly only: all three scoped fixes (E05-NB-1, E05-NB-2, E05-NB-5) are present in the working tree and re-verified by this pass, which supersedes the blocked envelope on substance. Not a code or spec issue.\"\n  ],\n  \"readinessAssessment\": \"Ready for closeout. The prior canonical review (002-epic-review.json) passed with zero blocking findings; this reverify converges on it. All three fix-batch-001 items verified applied against the current tree: package.json 'verify-all' now delegates to 'pnpm run verify' (E05-NB-1); PROMPT_NAMES (new, Object.keys(PROMPT_REGISTRY)) and DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES are exported through src/sdk.ts with the SDK-only export snapshot in test/retirement.test.ts intentionally extended per the fix-batch instruction, while PROMPT_REGISTRY itself stays internal (E05-NB-2); epic.md line 3 now reads Implemented and AC-5.3 carries the ratified ruling-020 conditional-landing qualifier matching the tech design's Flow 5 paragraph, and the obsolete Story 5 BLOCKED note is resolved (E05-NB-5). No fix-batch regressions found: the export change is snapshot-pinned, check-boundaries.mjs tightens the inference/-may-not-import-domains/ rule, both script names are preserved. Gates independently re-run: story gate (pnpm run verify) and epic gate (pnpm run verify-all) both green — exit 0, 40 test files, 377 passed, 9 env-gated keyed skips, exactly one visible 'NOT-RAN: real-inference (LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY unset)' accounting line, matching the canonical review's gate report. The keyed capstone receipt (2026-06-12, openai/gpt-4o-mini, 13/13, run twice) stands in the team-impl-log. Remaining confirmed items are non-blocking: two canonically-deferred observations (E05-NB-3 human-ruling at dial-in, E05-NB-4 cosmetic) and the team-impl-log Epic Closeout block, which closeout itself updates. The known pre-acceptance backfill obligation (prompt/model dial-in findings) and the manual-only keyed-path regression check remain accepted unresolved items, unchanged.\",\n  \"recommendedNextStep\": \"Proceed to closeout: update the team-impl-log Epic Closeout block (review artifact 002 pass, fix batch 001 applied and verified by reverify 003 notwithstanding the blocked 002-fix-result envelope, final gate pass 377 passed / 9 keyed-skipped), then commit the fix-batch working-tree changes. Carry E05-NB-3 and the dial-in backfill obligation into the post-epic dial-in working period; no further fix batch is needed.\"\n}\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":431,"cache_read_input_tokens":66025,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":431},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"n